GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A row of the excluded-facility list`
`the excluded-list rows numbered` n MEANS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `number` EQUALS n) `the excluded-facility list`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the province of excluded-list row` n MEANS
    CONSIDER `the excluded-list rows numbered` n
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r's `province`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no such excluded-list row`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of facilities on excluded-list row` n MEANS
    CONSIDER `the excluded-list rows numbered` n
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN count (r's `facilities`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no such excluded-list row`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of addresses on excluded-list row` n MEANS
    CONSIDER `the excluded-list rows numbered` n
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN count (r's `addresses`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no such excluded-list row`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no such excluded-list row` MEANS REFUSE "the excluded-facility list has no row of that number"

-- Whether a facility is named on the list, by its exact text as the list writes it. A facility the
-- list names under another spelling, or at another branch, is not found: a reader's aid only.
GIVEN `name` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`named on the excluded-facility list` `name` MEANS
    any (GIVEN r YIELD elem `name` (r's `facilities`)) `the excluded-facility list`
